<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 3.658 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 3.658 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.658 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    150 million    363 days</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    550 million     39 days</p>
<p>    600 million     31 days</p>
<p>    600 million     20 days</p>
<p>    650 million     10 days</p>
<p>    650 million	6 days</p>
<p>    158 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
